<section class="container" style="padding-block:4rem 2rem;max-width:760px;">
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">“Positioning” is usually understood as a self-image: what a company wants to stand for, which values it ascribes to itself, what character it intends for its brand. That is an internal matter and, as such, without consequence.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Here placement means something different — a <strong>location in the competitive field</strong>. Who are you actually compared against? On which shelf, in which tender, in which list of search results, in which procurement process? This location is an economic factor: it decides on listing, pricing latitude, sales effort — and on which arguments are heard at all.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">The wrong placement is expensive, even if everything else is done right.</p>
</section>

