<section class="container" style="padding-block:1rem 4rem;max-width:760px;">
  <h2 class="display-md reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Securing it means not hoping</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The difference between a positioning and a secured placement lies in testing. A position that is merely claimed lasts until the first counter-evidence — the first buyer meeting, the first shelf comparison, the first cease-and-desist letter.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Securing means anticipating each of these tests: the competitive comparison in the real environment, not on the mood board. Legal robustness before production, not after. The sales test before a range is rolled out. At Piasten, exactly this was the reason why some developments never made it into the range — the test took place, and it came out negative. That is not failure but the point of the exercise.</p>
</section>

